think Standfast first: read crux/REDS.md whole. Every living row (80, 83, 84, 85) and every prose note is CLOSED or released; #75 stays errata behind a custody gate (history rewrite, Keaton's hand) -- not agent-closable. No open agent-closable red blocks new work; the line is clear.
think Running thread: the newest log (edge_draw, 20260818.174459) landed the polygon OUTLINE by Bresenham and named a polygon FILL as a next sibling. Lindy-first crux-first among the three named siblings (Freeman chain code, nearest-template classifier, polygon fill): the fill is the direct completion of the outline just landed -- the outline/fill pair every chart bar, sprite, and UI panel needs -- and its crux (scanline vertex parity) is a real, decisive, solvable rasterization problem. Took the fill.
think Design crux -- vertex parity. A scanline that grazes a vertex must count it once, not twice or zero, or a whole row leaks or drops. Ruled the ambiguity out by construction: sample each pixel row at its HALF-INTEGER center in DOUBLED coordinates, so the sample line is ODD while every vertex sits on an EVEN one. No scanline ever lands on a vertex, so the even-odd count is always exact, and a horizontal edge (equal doubled y) never crosses an odd scanline -- naturally excluded, no special case.
think Compose not braid: fill_polygon draws the closed boundary through edge_draw.draw_line (so the outline is never broken and every vertex is validated -- VertexOutOfBounds refuses before any fill), then owns its interior scanline fill. The union is the solid shape. The boundary draw is necessary: half-integer sampling leaves the top/bottom rows short (a rectangle's row y=4 samples at 4.5, outside the span), and the Bresenham outline completes exactly those rows. This is sameness-is-the-macro made concrete -- shared put_pixel, is_set, lit_count, the white ink, the EmptySource/VertexOutOfBounds names, the same all-or-nothing bound as edge_draw; learning one is learning both.
think Bounds: canvas by qoi_max_pixels, the per-row crossing scratch by the vertex count (at most one crossing per edge), the scanline loop by the canvas height, x-intersection in i64 (coords <= 8192 doubled <= 16384, products tiny). All-or-nothing: a refusal fills nothing.
obs GREEN on the first full metal run -- no red booked. The rectangle fills a solid 6x4 block (24 pixels) where paint_polygon left it a hollow frame, the interior pixel (3,2) LIT, the fill a strict superset of the outline whose interior the outline lacks; the even-odd concavity crux holds -- a U-shape's arm row crosses the boundary four times (two spans, six lit with the notch dark) while its bar row crosses twice (one span, nine solid), the whole solid U 51 pixels (the 9x7 field minus the 3x4 notch); a triangle's span widens from apex to base; QOI round-trip byte-for-byte; EmptySource + VertexOutOfBounds refuse by name; determinism.
obs Rota lap deep-read foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md -- compress by public similarity. This rung is edge_draw's sibling by shape, sharing its helpers, ink, error names, and bound; a line saved by sameness is free forever, so the fill cost a page of prose, never a private dialect.
loom witness=fill_polygon_witness checks=1 build=green selftest=green
